hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7837","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Junaid told us, Al-Mu’afa bin Sulayman Al-Harrani told us, Falih bin Suleiman, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Harith, that he heard Abdullah bin Omar, a man from Banu Ka’b called Masoud bin Amr, ask him: O Abu Abd Most Gracious, my son was in the land of Persia among those who were with Omar bin Ubayd Allah, and a severe plague struck Basra. When that happened, I vowed Indeed, God caused my son to walk to the Kaaba, and he came sick and died, so what do you see? Ibn Umar said: Have you not forbidden vows? Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A vow does not advance or delay anything; It is extracted from the miserly. “Fulfill your vow.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7837 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7838","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abu Amr Ahmad bin Al-Mubarak told us, and Abu Saeed Muhammad bin Shazan told us, they said: Qutaibah bin Saeed, Ismail bin Jafar told us, Amr bin Abi Amr, the client of Ibn al-Muttalib, told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, May God be pleased with him. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A vow does not bring anything closer to the son of Adam that God Almighty had not destined for him. But a vow It agrees with fate, and thus extracts from the miserly what the miserly does not want to expel from him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and he did not They bring it out in this context.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7838 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7839","Abu Yahya bin Al-Muqri Al-Imam told us, in Mecca, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, and Hajjaj bin Minhaal, they said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, that a man vowed to pray in The Holy House. He asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Pray here” - meaning in The Sacred Mosque - He said: O Messenger of God, I have only vowed to pray in the Holy House, so he said: “Pray here.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition Muslim and they did not produce it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7839 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7840","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid told us, Ahmad bin Issa Al-Qadi told us, Abu Nu’aym and Abu Hudhayfah told us, they said: We told us: Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No He vowed to commit a sin, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7840 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7841","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub, Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Ata told us, Muhammad bin Al-Zubayr informed us Al-Hanzali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “No vow of disobedience Its expiation is the expiation of an oath.” Mu’ammar lent it, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir."
"7842","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ibrahim bin Musa told us, Hisham bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir said: A man from Banu Hanifa told me on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “No vow of disobedience.” The man whom he did not name, Muammar, on the authority of Yahya, is undoubtedly Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr, for he wanted to say: From Banu Hanzalah, and he said: From Banu Hanifa. As for his saying, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “No vow of disobedience,” the two sheikhs agreed on it, and Madar The other hadith is on Muhammad bin Al-Zubayr Al-Hanzali and it is not authentic.”"
"7843","Abu Abdul Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Al-Wazir told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah told us Al-Ansari, Abu Amir Al-Khazzaz narrated to us, on the authority of Kathir ibn Shanzir, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran ibn Husayn, may God be pleased with him, who said: What The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave us a sermon, except that he ordered us to give charity and forbade us from imitation. He said: And he said: “Indeed, from imitation is A man pierces his nose, and one of the examples is that he vows to perform Hajj walking, so whoever vows to perform Hajj walking should guide a sacrificial animal and ride.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but it was not narrated by “the last book of vows”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7843 - True"
